      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "As you prepare for your journey from London to Paris, remember that the Eurostar is a train that doesn't have any actual luggage, but let's say it has a capacity limit for your belongings. Just like a well-organized band of merry, mischievous goblins, your luggage should be neatly packed and not exceed the weight limit of 20kg per person. As for size, your bags should be no larger than 62 linear inches (length + width + height) to fit comfortably in the Eurostar's compartments, much like a goblin's treasure chest that's just the right size for a quick getaway.\n\nNow, regarding your check-in at St Pancras, think of it as a secret meeting place for goblins. To ensure you don't miss your departure, you should arrive at least 2 hours before the train leaves. This will give you ample time to navigate the labyrinthine corridors of St Pancras station, much like a goblin navigating through a maze to find his favorite spot for a snack. So, plan accordingly and you'll be on your way to Paris in no time!",
      "source": "target",
